=======================================================================
ZGA ORTHOGROUP CONSERVATION ANALYSIS 
=======================================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
This pipeline characterizes the evolutionary conservation of ZGA
(Zygotic Genome Activation) genes in Astrangia poculata by:
- Running OrthoFinder on two taxon sets
- Verifying orthogroup stability when outgroups are added
- Classifying ZGA genes as pan-metazoan, cnidarian-specific, or orphan

KEY FINDING
-----------
Cluster 2 (ZGA genes, n=365) are highly conserved across animals:
- 97.7% of orthogroups are stable across runs
- Only 1.6% (6/365) are Astrangia-specific orphans
- vs 4.7% orphan rate in background genes
→ ZGA genes are enriched for ancient, conserved gene families

